      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COMANCHE CHIEF (1) two career starts have been encouraging and looks to find his race today from the good barrier. Fanned five wide on the home turn with a battling fourth over 1300m at Warwick Farm in a Super Maiden. Blinkers go on and he should get the better of these. RED DEER (8) finally gave us a glimpse of what he's capable of when warming up late to secure third over 1500m at this track. Near his top now and look for him launching late. WARM FRONT (9) far from disgraced at his second run back with the 59kg when a tiring sixth over 1350m at Beaumont (Newcastle). Cross over nose band goes on and has the upside to figure prominently. POWER BROKER (2) went back from the outside draw on debut before producing a reasonable effort in the straight when fifth over 1300m at Warwick Farm. Sticky gate again and no surprise to see him run into the minor money.",
